rrent&nbsp;Address:&nbsp;12&nbsp;Franklin&nbsp;Street,&nbsp;Taneytown,&nbsp;Md&nbsp;21787&nbsp;(lives&nbsp;with&nbsp;aunt,&nbsp;Sharon&nbsp;Esworthy)</p><p></p><p>Child:&nbsp;&nbsp;Jacob&nbsp;Frye</p><p>DOB:&nbsp;4-12-10</p><p>Address:&nbsp;&nbsp;11433-A&nbsp;Haughs&nbsp;Church&nbsp;Rd.,&nbsp;Keymar,&nbsp;Md&nbsp;21757</p><p></p><p>Paternal&nbsp;Aunt&nbsp;/&nbsp;Caregiver:&nbsp;Sharon&nbsp;Esworthy</p><p>DOB:&nbsp;&nbsp;1-26-&nbsp;75</p><p>Address:&nbsp;12&nbsp;Franklin&nbsp;Street,&nbsp;Taneytown,&nbsp;Md&nbsp;21787</p><p>Phone:&nbsp;&nbsp;443-789-7649</p><p></p><p>Gary&nbsp;Esworthy&nbsp;(uncle)</p><p>DOB:&nbsp;10-26-1961</p><p>Address:&nbsp;12&nbsp;Franklin&nbsp;Street,&nbsp;Taneytown,&nbsp;Md&nbsp;21787</p><p></p><p><strong><u>Reported&nbsp;concern:</u></strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Sharon&nbsp;told&nbsp;referent&nbsp;that&nbsp;Makenzie&nbsp;can’t&nbsp;stay&nbsp;with&nbsp;her&nbsp;anymore,&nbsp;and&nbsp;dad&nbsp;doesn’t&nbsp;want&nbsp;her&nbsp;to&nbsp;come&nbsp;back&nbsp;to&nbsp;his&nbsp;home.&nbsp;&nbsp;Everything&nbsp;was&nbsp;fine&nbsp;on&nbsp;Saturday.&nbsp;&nbsp;All&nbsp;of&nbsp;a&nbsp;sudden&nbsp;&quot;all&nbsp;hell&nbsp;broke&nbsp;loose&quot;&nbsp;on&nbsp;Tuesday.&nbsp;&nbsp;Sharon&nbsp;went&nbsp;through&nbsp;Makenzie&#39;s&nbsp;phone&nbsp;and&nbsp;saw&nbsp;she&nbsp;was&nbsp;sending&nbsp;all&nbsp;kinds&nbsp;of&nbsp;inappropriate&nbsp;pictures&nbsp;and&nbsp;soliciting&nbsp;guys&nbsp;that&nbsp;were&nbsp;much&nbsp;older.&nbsp;Referent&nbsp;said&nbsp;that&nbsp;when&nbsp;Makenzie&nbsp;was&nbsp;12&nbsp;years&nbsp;old&nbsp;she&nbsp;left&nbsp;home&nbsp;and&nbsp;stayed&nbsp;at&nbsp;a&nbsp;18-19&nbsp;year&nbsp;old&nbsp;guys&nbsp;house.&nbsp;Referent&nbsp;said&nbsp;Makenzie&nbsp;was&nbsp;not&nbsp;given&nbsp;a&nbsp;phone&nbsp;at&nbsp;Sharon&#39;s&nbsp;house&nbsp;because&nbsp;of&nbsp;this.&nbsp;Makenzie&nbsp;visited&nbsp;her&nbsp;mother&nbsp;for&nbsp;lunch&nbsp;2&nbsp;weeks&nbsp;ago,&nbsp;and&nbsp;her&nbsp;mom&nbsp;gave&nbsp;her&nbsp;a&nbsp;phone&nbsp;because&nbsp;told&nbsp;her&nbsp;dad&nbsp;took&nbsp;her&nbsp;phone&nbsp;(did&nbsp;not&nbsp;allow&nbsp;her&nbsp;to&nbsp;have&nbsp;one).&nbsp;&nbsp;Sharon&nbsp;did&nbsp;not&nbsp;give&nbsp;her&nbsp;the&nbsp;phone.&nbsp;&nbsp;Bio&nbsp;mom&nbsp;did.</p><p></p><p>Months&nbsp;ago&nbsp;Sharon&nbsp;and&nbsp;Gary&nbsp;had&nbsp;a&nbsp;fridge&nbsp;with&nbsp;beer&nbsp;in&nbsp;it.&nbsp;They&nbsp;looked&nbsp;at&nbsp;it&nbsp;one&nbsp;day&nbsp;and&nbsp;noticed&nbsp;it&nbsp;was&nbsp;less&nbsp;in&nbsp;there&nbsp;and&nbsp;moved&nbsp;it&nbsp;to&nbsp;their&nbsp;bedroom.&nbsp;&nbsp;When&nbsp;they&nbsp;go&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;store,&nbsp;she&nbsp;sneaks&nbsp;into&nbsp;their&nbsp;bedroom,&nbsp;gets&nbsp;alcohol&nbsp;and&nbsp;drinks&nbsp;it.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p></p><p>Mental&nbsp;Health&nbsp;Diagnoses:&nbsp;&nbsp;Bipolar&nbsp;and&nbsp;ADHD&nbsp;were&nbsp;diagnosed&nbsp;in&nbsp;Frederick&nbsp;County.&nbsp;Her&nbsp;biological&nbsp;mother&nbsp;has&nbsp;a&nbsp;history&nbsp;(and&nbsp;family&nbsp;history)&nbsp;of&nbsp;bipolar.&nbsp;Makenzie&nbsp;stopped&nbsp;taking&nbsp;medicine&nbsp;in&nbsp;July&nbsp;because&nbsp;she&nbsp;refused&nbsp;to&nbsp;do&nbsp;virtual&nbsp;meetings.&nbsp;&nbsp;When&nbsp;she&nbsp;started&nbsp;mental&nbsp;health&nbsp;care&nbsp;in&nbsp;Carroll&nbsp;Co.,&nbsp;it&nbsp;was&nbsp;said&nbsp;she&nbsp;wasn’t&nbsp;bipolar,&nbsp;it&nbsp;was&nbsp;just&nbsp;her&nbsp;way&nbsp;of&nbsp;acting&nbsp;out.&nbsp;&nbsp;She&nbsp;currently&nbsp;sees&nbsp;a&nbsp;therapist&nbsp;in&nbsp;Westminster&nbsp;(unknown&nbsp;&nbsp;name&nbsp;but&nbsp;her&nbsp;aunt&nbsp;would&nbsp;know).&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p></p><p>Dad&nbsp;states&nbsp;he&nbsp;is&nbsp;willing&nbsp;to&nbsp;accept&nbsp;services&nbsp;but&nbsp;does&nbsp;not&nbsp;want&nbsp;Makenzie&nbsp;back&nbsp;in&nbsp;his&nbsp;home.&nbsp;</p><p></p><p>Referral&nbsp;will&nbsp;be&nbsp;forwarded&nbsp;as&nbsp;an&nbsp;outreach&nbsp;for&nbsp;services&nbsp;and&nbsp;forwarded&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;CCAIC&nbsp;re:&nbsp;the&nbsp;inappropriate&nbsp;pictures&nbsp;being&nbsp;sent.</p><p></p><p><strong>Family&nbsp;Preservation&nbsp;Supervisor,&nbsp;J.Miller,&nbsp;contacted&nbsp;Mr.&nbsp;Frye&nbsp;who&nbsp;stated&nbsp;that&nbsp;his&nbsp;daughter&nbsp;is&nbsp;back&nbsp;in&nbsp;his&nbsp;care&nbsp;and&nbsp;he&nbsp;is&nbsp;not&nbsp;in&nbsp;need&nbsp;of&nbsp;additional&nbsp;services&nbsp;from&nbsp;the&nbsp;Department&nbsp;at&nbsp;this&nbsp;time.&nbsp;Supportive&nbsp;services&nbsp;were&nbsp;offered/explained.&nbsp;</strong></p><p></p><p>[Carroll&nbsp;County&nbsp;is&nbsp;screening&nbsp;this&nbsp;out&nbsp;on&nbsp;behalf&nbsp;of&nbsp;Frederick&nbsp;County&nbsp;as&nbsp;they&nbsp;were&nbsp;not&nbsp;able&nbsp;to&nbsp;due&nbsp;to&nbsp;a&nbsp;CJAMS&nbsp;glitch.]</p>",
